{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#129","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#129","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#129\",\"parent_revision\":\"fd4f3fbe688b5f62d736c998a0c73aa3f1ceec3f68105130514b51cd62a7555b\",\"root_revision\":\"fd4f3fbe688b5f62d736c998a0c73aa3f1ceec3f68105130514b51cd62a7555b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSince #108, `generate_docs_url` returns a CLI invocation \u2014 `skilllint rule <CODE>` \u2014 not a URL. `ValidationIssue.docs_url` carries that same value.\\n\\nBoth names now describe something the code no longer produces.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why It Was Not Renamed In 103\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRoughly 80 call sites, plus `docs_url` is a public field on a frozen dataclass that the reporters and the JSON output consume. Renaming it changes machine-readable output that downstream consumers may parse.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What This Needs\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nIts own PR with a deprecation path for the field name, rather than being folded into unrelated work.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #108 \u2014 replaced URLs with `skilllint rule <CODE>`\\n- #103 \u2014 widened the annotation, deliberately deferred the rename\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d27629095891bed0179bcfc6a6b4c9bbc5edca8cab47b42f20a31aa647b639e2\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-7QA\"}"}